A node handle's type is the component it was written on, and the shake walked
that component whole: `#d` on a ui.datepicker, never read, kept every helper
gtk4's datepicker body calls -- LookOf, CssOf, CrossOf, TextAlignOf and the
Style they take -- in a model.go with no call to any of them. Without `#d`
none was written. A component named as a type keeps its props' types; what
instantiates it walks the rest.

deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `func (LookOf|LookHidden|CssOf|CrossOf|TextAlignOf|LineOf)\(` -- a handle's type calls nothing
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `type Style struct` -- nothing builds a Style once the body is folded

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        gtk4
    }
}

ui.window(title="t") {
    ui.datepicker #d()
}
-- out/go/gtk4/callbacks.go --
// Code generated by sngl (gtk4) from app.sngl; DO NOT EDIT.

package main

import "duckfam.us/sngl/pkg/go/gtk4rt"

func main() {
	gtk4rt.Init()
	m := New()
	m.buildWidgetTree()
	gtk4rt.RunWindows(true)
}
